## F-12: a `for (i, x) in ...` tuple pattern binds fresh names even when an
## outer `i` is already in scope. The loop's `i` used to resolve to the outer
## binding, so the loop saw the outer value (and the outer type).

def main
  let i = "outer"
  let pairs: Array[(Int, Int)] = [(1, 10), (2, 20)]
  for (i, x) in pairs
    puts "#{i + 1}:#{x}"
  end
  puts i
end
